### Theory: jQuery Selection Performance

```javascript
// Efficient - specific selector
$('#main')                      // ID lookup (fastest)
$('.container')                 // Class lookup
$('div')                        // Element lookup
$('[href="url"]')               // Attribute lookup

// Less efficient - complex selectors
$('div > p:first')              // Multiple iterations
$('*')                          // All elements
$(':visible')                   // Visibility check

// Performance tips:
// ✓ Use specific selectors
// ✓ Cache selections
// ✓ Use ID when possible
// ✓ Avoid universal selector
// ✓ Minimize re-selection

// Bad: Re-selecting in loop
for (let i = 0; i < 1000; i++) {
    $('.item').append('text');  // Selects every time!
}

// Good: Select once
const $items = $('.item');
for (let i = 0; i < 1000; i++) {
    $items.append('text');
}
```

