### Application 3: Infinite Scroll Pagination

**Theory:** Dynamically loads content as user scrolls, eliminating traditional pagination and improving engagement.

**Process Flow:**
```
Scroll Event → Calculate Distance to Bottom → 
AJAX Load More Data → Append to DOM → Reset Scroll Check
```

**Implementation:**

```javascript
class InfiniteScroll {
    constructor(options = {}) {
        this.page = 1;
        this.isLoading = false;
        this.hasMore = true;
        this.container = options.container || '#items-container';
        this.apiUrl = options.apiUrl || '/api/items';
        this.threshold = options.threshold || 200;
        
        this.init();
    }

    init() {
        $(window).on('scroll', () => this.checkScroll());
        this.loadMore();
    }

    checkScroll() {
        // Theory: Calculate distance from bottom
        const scrollTop = $(window).scrollTop();
        const docHeight = $(document).height();
        const windowHeight = $(window).height();
        const distanceFromBottom = docHeight - (scrollTop + windowHeight);

        // Load when near bottom
        if (distanceFromBottom < this.threshold && !this.isLoading && this.hasMore) {
            this.loadMore();
        }
    }

    loadMore() {
        if (this.isLoading || !this.hasMore) return;

        this.isLoading = true;
        this.showLoader();

        $.ajax({
            url: this.apiUrl,
            data: { page: this.page },
            dataType: 'json',
            timeout: 10000,
            success: (response) => {
                if (response.items.length === 0) {
                    this.hasMore = false;
                    this.showEnd();
                } else {
                    this.appendItems(response.items);
                    this.page++;
                }
            },
            error: () => this.showError('Load failed'),
            complete: () => {
                this.hideLoader();
                this.isLoading = false;
            }
        });
    }

    appendItems(items) {
        const $items = $(items.map(item => `
            <div class="item-card" data-id="${item.id}">
                <img src="${item.image}">
                <h3>${item.title}</h3>
            </div>
        `).join(''));

        $(this.container).append($items);
        $items.hide().fadeIn(400);
    }

    showLoader() {
        if ($('#loader').length === 0) {
            $(this.container).after('<div id="loader"><div class="spinner"></div></div>');
        }
    }

    hideLoader() {
        $('#loader').hide();
    }

    showEnd() {
        $(this.container).after('<div class="text-center">No more items</div>');
    }

    showError(msg) {
        $(this.container).after(`<div class="alert alert-danger">${msg}</div>`);
    }
}

$(document).ready(function() {
    new InfiniteScroll({
        container: '#products',
        apiUrl: '/api/products',
        threshold: 300
    });
});
```

**Theory Explanation:**
- **Scroll Detection**: Continuous monitoring of scroll position
- **Throttling**: `isLoading` flag prevents duplicate requests
- **Lazy Loading**: Only loads visible content, improves performance
- **Error Handling**: Gracefully handles load failures
- **User Engagement**: Seamless loading improves session time

